{
  "id": "proj-shoe-rack-bench",
  "slug": "shoe-rack-bench",
  "status": "published",
  "title": "Shoe Rack Bench",
  "summary": "A hallway bench with slatted shoe shelves underneath. Sit down, take your boots off, done.",
  "difficulty": "beginner",
  "estimatedHours": 4,
  "imageUrl": null,
  "currency": "USD",
  "steps": [
    "From the 2x2s cut four 17 1/4 in legs, six 35 in long rails and six 11 in short rails. From the 1x4s cut sixteen 14 in shelf slats, and from the 1x6s three 40 in seat boards.",
    "Drill one pocket hole in each end of every rail, set on the jig for 1 1/2 in stock.",
    "Build two end frames: glue and screw three short rails between a pair of legs, at the top and with their top edges 3 in and 9 in up from the floor.",
    "Join the end frames with the long rails at the same three heights, front and back. Check the frame is square by measuring both diagonals.",
    "Lay eight slats across the long rails of each lower level, front to back, spaced evenly. Glue and screw each slat down with one 1 1/4 in screw at each end.",
    "Screw figure-8 fasteners into shallow recesses on top of the top rails, set the three seat boards on with a 1 in overhang all round, and screw up through the fasteners into the seat. They let the boards move with the seasons.",
    "Sand from 80 to 220 grit, break the edges, and apply two coats of polyurethane. Stick felt pads under the legs."
  ],
